              "type": "Type"
            }
          ],
          "content": "The numerous old men that Rembrandt etched in his early years in Leiden will have regularly posed for him while seated in a chair. This is rarely visible in his prints, but is so in this one. The shabbily attired old man with a patchy beard and bony hands stands out slightly against the large armchair in which he sits. This chair lends him an air of near biblical grandeur."
        },
        {
          "type": "LinguisticObject",
          "classified_as": [
